# KEY|what it is and what the kit uses it for|where to get it|after|when
VPN_PROVIDER|All torrent traffic goes through this VPN, never your home connection. ProtonVPN supports port forwarding (more peers, faster downloads); NordVPN doesn't.|||
TS_NODE_media|The media apps' address on your tailnet: https://<name>.<your-tailnet>.ts.net. It must be unique in your tailnet.|||
EXPOSE_media|funnel: Seerr (requests only, behind its own login) is reachable from the public internet, so friends can ask for movies and shows without Tailscale. tailnet: only your Tailscale devices can reach it.|||
TS_NODE_dashboard|The Homarr dashboard's address on your tailnet: https://<name>.<your-tailnet>.ts.net. Never public.|||
HOMARR_INTEGRATIONS|on: connect Homarr's widgets to each app automatically. off: only create the app tiles.|||
VPN_COUNTRIES|Which countries Gluetun picks VPN servers in, comma-separated (the provider's country names).|||
MEDIA_SUBNET|The private network the media apps share inside Docker. Change it only if it clashes with a network this Mac already uses; qBittorrent skips its login for the Mac itself through this network's first address.|||
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY|WireGuard is how Gluetun connects to your VPN; this key ties the connection to your VPN account.|account.protonvpn.com → Downloads → WireGuard configuration. Under VPN options turn on NAT-PMP (port forwarding), pick a P2P server (double-arrow icon), create the file and copy its PrivateKey value.||VPN_PROVIDER=protonvpn
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY|WireGuard (NordLynx) is how Gluetun connects to your VPN; this key ties the connection to your NordVPN account.|Nord Account → NordVPN → Manual setup → generate an access token, then run this in Terminal and copy the nordlynx_private_key value:\ncurl -s -u token:<TOKEN> https://api.nordvpn.com/v1/users/services/credentials||VPN_PROVIDER=nordvpn
TS_AUTHKEY|Tailscale is a private network linking your devices. The kit uses it for remote access to the dashboard and apps, and Funnel for the few pages meant to be public.|Tailscale admin console → Settings → Keys → Generate auth key. Make it Reusable and Pre-approved, not Ephemeral. It's only used for each node's first login, so its expiry (up to 90 days) only has to outlast the install.||
HOMARR_API_KEY|Homarr is the dashboard. The kit uses this key to add a tile and widget for each app.|Open the dashboard, create your admin account, then create an API key under Management → Tools → API. It's shown once, as <id>.<token>. Put it in ~/server/secrets.conf and run ./kit install again.|after|
